   "evidence": "tune traditional German (Hänschen klein, credited to Franz Wiedemann, 1821-1882); English words anonymous, printed in 1854 (Mason and Webb, The Song-book of the School-room) and in school songbooks of 1914-1915 (SingPraises.net lists the author as Unknown, no copyright)"
  },
  "lyrics": "1. Lightly row, lightly row, o'er the glassy waves we go; Smoothly glide, smoothly glide, on the silent tide. Let the winds and waters be mingled with our melody; Sing and float, sing and float, in our little boat.",
  "notes": [
   "Curriculum song (Prep A, prep-a.allegro). \"Lightly Row\": the German folk tune of \"Hänschen klein\" (credited to Franz Wiedemann, 1821-1882) with anonymous English words, printed in Lowell Mason and George Webb's \"The Song-book of the School-room\" (1854) and in many school songbooks since (Hollis Dann's \"First Year Music\", 1914; \"The Golden Book of Favorite Songs\", 1915); public domain. Our own arrangement, in C position for the right hand. It replaces When the Saints Go Marching In, deleted from the library (Oct 20, 2026): a quick, bright song made of skips (G-E, F-D) for Unit 7's Allegro."
  ],
  "source": {
   "site": "Piano-Master",
   "url": "https://github.com/tedc7/Piano-Master/blob/main/content/pieces/lightly-row.yaml"
  },
  "sourceIds": [],
  "tempoSource": "Allegro, as the skill it practises asks: quarter = 116, the curriculum's quick tempo (When the Saints, which it replaces, was 112)"
 },
